WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.734
-It is great to see you.
-It is so good to see you.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:06.300
-You know what I miss
about you?

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.133
-What?
-A lot. But your laugh.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.667
I love your laugh.
-It's a lot.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.534
-You have a great laugh.
-It's a cackle.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.734
It is a cackle.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:18.033
-When it eventually,
you don't fake it.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:22.300
So, yeah.
-It is honestly it is karma.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.367
This is my mom's laugh.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:28.200
And as a child,
I tormented her over her laugh.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.067
Whenever I was doing a school
play or something, I was like,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.067
"I always know where you are
in the theater, mom.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.100
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.634
Like,
just tone it down a little bit."

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.467
-Then look at you,
now you have it.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.100
Your kids know
when you are laughing?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.167
-Yeah, and they are just
as annoyed as I am.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.467
-You are an amazing actor.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.534
And I told you this right
before the show,

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.334
but I want to tell you again.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:55.467
Some of the best directing --
you directed "The Mandalorian"

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.267
and "The Book of Boba Fett."

00:00:57.267 --> 00:01:00.767
You are amazing. Fantastic.
I mean, congrats.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:03.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.167
-It's incredible
working for Jon Favreau.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.467
-Jon Favreau is great too,
he's a genius.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.634
-But I worked with you.
You directed me in a movie.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:11.701
-Last time we saw each other,

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.467
I was interviewing
you for hours.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.133
-Yeah. It was fun though.
-Yeah, you were amazing.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.968
-And I watched this episode.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.334
It was crazy.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.934
As I was watching I am like,
"who directed this

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.667
because this is really --"
and you did it.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.200
You hit a home run, buddy.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.634
What is it like to direct
a "Star Wars" project?

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.367
-It's incredible.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.200
But for me personally, it is all
the more meaningful

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.667
because I was very lucky.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:40.133
I got to grow up basically
on my dad's movie sets

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.200
and George Lucas.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.000
Since my dad was 17,
George Lucas has been

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.234
my dad's mentor.
Because my Dad did --

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:47.434
-"American Graffiti."
-"American Graffiti."

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.634
Yeah, exactly.
-I mean, come on.

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:52.067
-Exactly, and George has kids
the same age

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:54.367
as all of the kids in my family.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.868
So we were all kind of raised
together.

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:59.968
And then I actually went to
summer camp

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:03.868
with Natalie Portman
before she did the prequels.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.801
And because I knew George,
and all that kind of stuff,

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.801
I got to go visit
a bunch on the prequels.

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:11.467
And so it's a very
personal thing

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:14.934
that I feel very protective of.
Of "Star Wars."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.300
-The "Star Wars."
-Of the "Star Wars."

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:23.067
-So when you you get involved
with that, and asked to do that,

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.267
did you ask George?

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.334
Did you ask --how did you get
in that world,

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:27.734
and like, "Hey,
I would like a shot at this."

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.033
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.334
So what happened is,
I just finished filming

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.167
"Jurassic World:
Fallen Kingdom,"

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.100
which is the movie before the
one that came out today.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.868
-Whoo!
-Why thank you.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:42.734
My dad started to direct
on "Solo."

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:46.901
And I was like, "Can I stay in
the UK and shadow you, please?"

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.267
And he said, "No."

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:52.234
And I just kind of begged
and pleaded and said,

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.067
"I'll just be very quiet on set,

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.968
and nobody will realize
I am there."

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.400
-Just try not to laugh.
-Yeah, just don't laugh.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.067
I don't think
I was successful at that.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:06.667
And so I got to go and shadow
and learn from him.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.100
It was incredible as well.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.133
Because I hadn't seen him
direct onset since I was a kid.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.601
And now being an actor,

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.434
and having had a couple
of decades doing this.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:17.334
I am like, "oh, wow.
You are really good."

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.567
-He knows how to do it, yeah.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:19.868
-And so, I met folks there.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:24.501
They brought me aboard
to write something.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:28.567
And that's how I started to get
to know the folks at Lucasfilm.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.567
-Cause Lucasfilm,
they also develop new stuff

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:32.901
people even haven't seen.

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.868
They're just working on ideas
on the next thing.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.601
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-But you directed Baby Yoda.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.033
-Oh, yeah.
I get to do that, yeah.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.701
-But Baby Yoda is real though?
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:46.767
-Baby Yoda is totally real,
totally real -- completely.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:50.667
One of the reasons why Jon
Favreau was so supportive of me

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:54.133
working with the legacy team
that developed

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.968
Baby Yoda,
was because I met them

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.701
and worked with them
both "Terminator"

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:00.133
and the original
"Jurassic World."

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.601
And so I knew
that team of puppeteers.

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.167
-It's amazing what they do.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:11.400
That little thing is probably
the cutest thing

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.634
I think I have ever seen,
besides my own children.

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:17.234
[ Laughter ]
You know, it's so cute.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.667
I go, "please do another scene
with Baby Yoda."

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:21.901
I love him so much.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.234
-I mean, I concur.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.467
Yeah.
Baby Yoda is the best.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.267
-You just fall
in love with him.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.667
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:33.834
And that's why Baby Yoda
has a lot of protection onset.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:37.901
Because we all are just looking
at Baby Yoda all the time.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.033
Being like, "I just want to
take that Baby Yoda."

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.434
It's very visceral.
You know?

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.234
-Just squeeze it. And I go, "I
love you. You're so cute."

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.200
-Did you know,
this might be wrong,

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.367
but this is what I've heard,
that the violence part of your

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.634
brain is right next to the cute
part of your brain.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.067
So when you think
something's really cute,

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.534
it bumps up against the violence
part of your brain, you're like,

00:04:56.534 --> 00:04:57.834
"I just want to
smush it to death."

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:58.868
[ Laughter ]
-Is that right?

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.167
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:01.367
-That's what I heard.
-I did not know that.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.767
-That's why if you see
something really cute,

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:07.634
it becomes, like at a certain
point, very gruesome.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:09.267
"I just want to smother it.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.534
[ Laughter ]
I'm just gonna --"

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:11.868
-Yeah. Yeah.
It's so cute, yeah.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:14.601
-"Push it down."
You know.

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:17.234
-You were saying that you are
a big "Star Wars" fan.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.701
And I go, "Yes,
I agree with you."

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.834
You had something painted
on the side of your house.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.434
-Yeah.
-I just go, "This is cool."

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:26.467
And you were nice enough
to take a photo.

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:28.067
-It is a mural on the side

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:32.334
of my house of the twin suns
of Tatooine.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:36.400
-That's "Star Wars" next level.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.334
I mean, how did the family --
-I begged. I begged.

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.734
My husband was supportive.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:44.868
My kids are like,
"What are you doing, mom?

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:48.467
On the side of our house?"

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.534
-I love that.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.567
-Can't get enough of it.
I love it.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:53.834
-Can we talk about
"Jurassic World."

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:56.501
-Yes, please.
Our movie.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:57.901
Our franchise.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.033
-That's right.
That's correct.

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.801
-Gyrosphere guy, everyone.
-Thank you.

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:03.534
Please hold your applause.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:05.634
Oh, you are.
That's interesting, oh you are.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.868
I was in, if you don't remember,
please hold your applause --

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.634
-How could you forget?
-Would you forget?

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:10.901
Apparently our audience did,

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:13.567
but I was in the first
"Jurassic World."

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:16.234
I was there.
I was the gyrosphere --

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:20.868
-Gyrosphere.
-Gyrosphere scientist guy.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:22.868
We had Chris Pratt on,
and I said,

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:25.968
"I was thinking
of reprising my character."

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:29.701
And he goes, "Your 'character'?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:32.133
He goes,
"You played you in that movie."

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.200
But, yeah, either way.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.934
-No small actors,
only small parts.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:40.634
-But we created a dynasty,
you and I.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.934
-Yes. Just us.
-In "Jurassic World."

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:45.400
Basically just us,
and here we are -- reunited.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.634
Like, we're labeling this show
"The Reunion" --

00:06:47.634 --> 00:06:49.367
-Oh!
-Because we are back together.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:51.667
-Because it's finally.
-Finally --

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:54.434
Jeff Goldblum, Laura Dern.
That's all good and funny.

00:06:54.434 --> 00:06:55.801
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.200
-When's Jimmy and Bryce
going to get back together?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.901
Because we weren't even
in the scene together.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:01.467
-I know, we should eventise it.
You know?

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:03.234
-We should. We are.

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:05.000
People are glued.
-They are clamoring for this.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.234
-"They're like, "Jimmy, are you
going to do another voiceover

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:08.667
for a LEGO video game?"

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:09.734
"Yeah."

00:07:09.734 --> 00:07:13.567
"An unlockable character?"
"Sure."

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:15.033
Why would you want
to unlock my character?

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.467
But you can unlock it.

00:07:17.467 --> 00:07:19.934
I give facts about dinosaurs.
-Very cool.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.567
-But this one is kind of --
this is the end.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.200
-Yeah, it's the conclusion.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.200
It is the epic conclusion
of the "Jurassic" franchise

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.801
that started
all of those years ago.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.133
[ Audience aws ]
-But it pays off.

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:32.834
Everyone's story pays off.

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:36.200
-Yeah, I mean, it's really
incredible to get to be

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.634
a part of this franchise

00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:40.701
that has spanned
such an immense amount of time.

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:44.133
And to have Laura Dern,
and Jeff Goldblum,

00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:48.234
and Sam Neil, and B.D. Wong,back
in this movie with all of us.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:51.000
And it's not --
it's an ensemble.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.200
This is all of our movie.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.534
They don't have cameos.

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:57.501
This is their movie as much
as it is any of ours.

00:07:57.501 --> 00:07:58.968
It was a blast.

00:07:58.968 --> 00:08:01.334
-And you see you guys all
on the screen then you hear --

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:05.934
and I am like, [Vocalizes]
"Don't cry, Jimmy. Don't cry.

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:07.467
You were in this movie
at one point. Remember?"

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:08.567
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:10.434
-I go, "Look what you guys
have become.

00:08:10.434 --> 00:08:12.834
I remember when you
were this tall."

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:15.467
-Stay jaded. Stay jaded.
-Stay jaded.

00:08:15.467 --> 00:08:17.968
When I did the first "Jurassic
World" everyone was this tall.

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:19.701
And I was like, "Oh, so cute,
Chris Pratt.

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:22.033
You're going to
grow up one day."

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:24.734
And then look at you guys now,
I'm watching on the IMAX.

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:25.834
-You know what's crazy?

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:28.968
When Chris Pratt
did the first Jurassic,

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:31.434
"Guardians of the Galaxy"
had not come out yet.

00:08:31.434 --> 00:08:34.133
So he was the guy
from "Parks and Rec."

00:08:34.133 --> 00:08:36.267
When he was doing the first
"Jurassic World."

00:08:36.267 --> 00:08:38.667
And he was like, "Oh, I hope
this thing I did,

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:40.434
"Guardians" works out."

00:08:40.434 --> 00:08:41.734
And I was like, 'Dude,
you are Starlord.

00:08:41.734 --> 00:08:43.033
It is going to be incredible."

00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:45.667
-It worked out pretty well.
-Yeah, I'll say.

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:47.067
So, it's just awesome.

00:08:47.067 --> 00:08:48.968
It's been incredible
getting to go on this journey.

00:08:48.968 --> 00:08:51.300
Because this has been --
these eight years

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.601
have really represented
so much in all of our lives.

00:08:53.601 --> 00:08:56.133
-Eight years. It's awesome.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:56.133 --> 00:08:58.667
Here's Bryce Dallas Howard
in "Jurassic World: Dominion."

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:01.000
Take a look at this.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.367
[ Dinosaur roars ]

00:09:05.367 --> 00:09:06.801
-[ Grunts, groans ]

00:09:06.801 --> 00:09:09.667
[ Dinosaur roars ]

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:10.868
Aah!

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:12.167
[ Dinosaur roaring ]
[ Panting ]

00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:17.167
♪♪

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:18.767
[ Bell tolling ]

00:09:18.767 --> 00:09:20.567
[ Breathing heavily ]

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:21.634
[ Grunts ]

00:09:21.634 --> 00:09:24.234
[ Dinosaur roars ]

00:09:24.234 --> 00:09:25.767
-That's what I am talking
about.

00:09:25.767 --> 00:09:27.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is how you do it, buddy.

00:09:27.634 --> 00:09:29.033
Bryce Dallas Howard, everybody.

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:32.634
"Jurassic World: Dominion"
is in theaters and IMAX today.

